Be very careful. He is advocating the protection racket which most of
the time is not the best strategy. This is from the mouth of a pro
who was one of the first to do the protection racket, who can do it
with almost any class, and who still plays with the pacifist conduct.
Don't do the racket unless you like a challenge or mini conduct. A
modified racket is better for the weak combat classes, or you decide
you want to do a bare handed arch or tourist and not throw any
weapons. Then go ahead, since you will need the AC for your
challenge. 

Here is how to do a modified racket, which can be ok for some of the
weaker hp classes. (arch,tourist, wiz, priest,knight ranger,
especially any elves playing these roles.) If you have a dwarf arch
with high con, play like this until you find decent armor and then
ditch the racket.

Explore and kill monsters, but let you pet level up too.Keep going
until level 3 or 4 and stop. Then let you pet kill most things while
you kill things only when absolutely necessary. Go to sokobon.

To conserve food pray every other eating period for food. Wait until
weak. Mark all shops on the way. Mark all levels with vaults

Do sokobon and get the goodies.Be careful on the last level. If you
have 4 dogs and cats at this point maxed out then fine, but if not
then you may have to help them take out the giant mimics. They can be
put to sleep and if you have a stethoscope you can help by attacking
them. (killing them yourself usually shoots you up a level.)


 On the way back to the mines use your pet to rob the shops of all
gold. 

If you find a pick axe soon in the mines go back and get the vault
gold. 

Go to mind town and donate gold. Keep some to set up some more shop
robbing with your pet. Be careful and lock the watch captain up if
you can, or if there is a leash or magic whistle in one of the shops
buy it and keep your pet away from the captain. Then rob all the
shops in minetown. The candle shop can get to be a pain since candles
don't give a lot of dough, but you can still get it all by selling
and reselling the candles. 

This should get you to naked AC 1, but if you are naked 5 or less,
consider this good enough and start killing things again. 




